# review: land after fixes by claude-sonnet-5.5 (session 2)
system/usr/share/bash-completion/completions/agent:8: blocking: The command list is globbed from "${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}/../../../../../bin". That resolves to the repo's bin/ only when the file is read in place under system/. Installed at /usr/share/bash-completion/completions it resolves to /bin, which works only if bin is a /usr/bin merge and the scripts are installed there. From a sysext or confext under /usr, bin is wherever the image puts it. A symlink in ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions resolves to ~/../../bin, so it finds nothing. BASH_SOURCE is not resolved through the symlink. — First-word completion silently returns nothing in the install cases the brief names. Resolve the symlink with readlink -f, or better, find the commands via PATH with compgen -c agent- (or 'agent help'), and strip the prefix. That works for every install layout.
system/usr/share/bash-completion/completions/agent:18: should-fix: The verdict case sources "$_agent_completion_dir/agent-verdict", the sibling completion file. This breaks when the symlink install links only the `agent` file, because the sibling is not next to the symlink. It also breaks if the directory is resolved differently. Bash-completion's own lazy loader (_completion_loader agent-verdict) is the normal way to load it. — Completion after 'agent verdict' fails when the sibling file is not beside the symlink. Try _completion_loader agent-verdict first and fall back to the sibling file, resolved with readlink -f.
bin/agent:10: should-fix: The help list prints full script names ('agent-doctor') under the header 'use: agent <command>'. The summary is only the first line of a comment, so multi-line summaries are cut mid-sentence: agent-reconcile ends 'did', and agent-run ends 'One session at a time,'. The brief said every script gets a true one-line summary on line 2, but these two were not fixed. — The first screen a human sees is inconsistent and truncated. Print the name without the 'agent-' prefix, and give reconcile and run a complete one-line summary.
bin/agent-layer:3: should-fix: The new 'Usage:' line was added but the old line-2 usage and description were left below. The per-command help now says 'Build one extension layer...' and then repeats 'Build one extension layer ... only when stale.'. agent-harvest and agent-new have the same duplicated or blank-separated lead. — 'agent help layer' reads redundantly. Drop the duplicate sentence. The change also touches a comment block the brief said to change only on line 2.
bin/agent:35: nit: 'agent --help' and 'agent -h' are treated as an unknown command and exit 2 with an error. 'agent help foo bar' is reported as unknown command 'foo bar'. — A human's first guess at help gets an error message. Treat them as 'help' and exit 0.
test/agent.test.sh:1: nit: The completion tests presumably only run the file in place under system/. No test covers an installed layout or a symlink. — This is how the path bug above went unnoticed. Add a case that copies or symlinks the completion into a temp dir.
